  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ الْحُسَيْنِ بْنِ مُوسَى بْنِ بَابَوَيْهِ الْقُمِّيُّ الْفَقِيهُ نَزِيلُ الرَّيِّ مُصَنِّفُ هَذَا الْكِتَابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ وَأَرْضَاهُ رَاهُ رُوِيَ عَنْ شُعَيْبِ بْنِ وَاقِدٍ عَنِ الْحُسَيْنِ بْنِ زَيْدٍ عَنِ الصَّادِقِ جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ عَنْ أَبِيهِ ، عَنْ آبَائِهِ عَنْ أَمِيرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ أَبِي طَالِبٍ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ قَالَ:",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Al-Husayn ibn Musa ibn Babawayh Al-Qummi, the jurist residing in Rayy and the author of this book (may Allah be pleased with him and grant him satisfaction), narrated from Shu'ayb ibn Waqid, from Al-Husayn ibn Zayd, from Al-Sadiq Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his forefathers, from Commander of the Faithful Ali ibn Abi Talib (peace be upon him), who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "نَهَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ عَنِ الْأَكْلِ عَلَى الْجَنَابَةِ وَقَالَ «إِنَّهُ يُورِثُ الْفَقْرَ» وَ نَهَى عَنْ تَقْلِيمِ الْأَظْفَارِ بِالْأَسْنَانِ وَ عَنِ السِّوَاكِ فِي الْحَمَّامِ وَ التَّنَخُّعِ فِي الْمَسَاجِدِ وَ نَهَى عَنْ أَكْلِ سُؤْرِ الْفَأْرَةِ وَقَالَ «لَا تَجْعَلُوا الْمَسَاجِدَ طُرُقًا حَتَّى تُصَلُّوا فِيهَا رَكْعَتَيْنِ» وَ نَهَى أَنْ يَبُولَ أَحَدٌ تَحْتَ شَجَرَةٍ مُثْمِرَةٍ أَوْ عَلَى قَارِعَةِ الطَّرِيقِ وَ نَهَى أَنْ يَأْكُلَ الْإِنْسَانُ بِشِمَالِهِ وَ أَنْ يَأْكُلَ وَ هُوَ مُتَّكِئٌ وَ نَهَى أَنْ تُجَصَّصَ الْمَقَابِرُ وَ يُصَلَّى فِيهَا وَقَالَ «إِذَا اغْتَسَلَ أَحَدُكُمْ فِي فَضَاءٍ مِنَ الْأَرْضِ فَلْيُحَاذِرْ عَلَى عَوْرَتِهِ وَلَا يَشْرَبَنَّ أَحَدُكُمُ الْمَاءَ مِنْ عِنْدِ عُرْوَةِ الْإِنَاءِ فَإِنَّهُ مُجْتَمَعُ الْوَسَخِ» وَ نَهَى أَنْ يَبُولَ أَحَدٌ فِي الْمَاءِ الرَّاكِدِ فَإِنَّهُ مِنْهُ يَكُونُ ذَهَابُ الْعَقْلِ وَ نَهَى أَنْ يَمْشِيَ الرَّجُلُ فِي فَرْدِ نَعْلٍ أَوْ أَنْ يَتَنَعَّلَ وَ هُوَ قَائِمٌ وَ نَهَى أَنْ يَبُولَ الرَّجُلُ وَ فَرْجُهُ بَادٍ لِلشَّمْسِ أَوْ لِلْقَمَرِ وَقَالَ «إِذَا دَخَلْتُمُ الْغَائِطَ فَتَجَنَّبُوا الْقِبْلَةَ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) forbade eating while in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) and said: 'It leads to poverty.' He forbade trimming nails with teeth, using the miswak in the bathhouse, and spitting in mosques. He forbade eating the leftovers of a mouse and said: 'Do not make the mosques pathways; rather, pray two units of prayer in them before passing through.' He prohibited urinating under fruit-bearing trees or on public roads. He forbade eating with the left hand and eating while reclining. He forbade plastering graves and praying upon them. He said: 'If one of you bathes in an open area, let him guard his private parts, and do not drink water from the handle of a container, for it is where dirt accumulates.' He prohibited urinating in stagnant water, saying, 'It causes the loss of intellect.' He forbade walking with only one shoe or putting on shoes while standing. He forbade a man from urinating while his private parts are exposed to the sun or the moon. He said: 'When you enter the place of relieving yourself, avoid facing the qiblah.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "و نَهَى عَنِ الرَّنَّةِ عِنْدَ الْمُصِيبَةِ وَ نَهَى عَنِ النِّيَاحَةِ وَ الِاسْتِمَاعِ إِلَيْهَا وَ نَهَى عَنْ اِتِّبَاعِ النِّسَاءِ الْجَنَائِزَ وَ نَهَى أَنْ يُحَى شَيْءٌ مِنْ كِتَابِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ بِالْبُزَاقِ أَوْ يُكْتَبَ بِهِ وَ نَهَى أَنْ يَكْذِبَ الرَّجُلُ فِي رُؤْيَاهُ مُتَعَمِّدًا وَقَالَ «يُكَلِّفُهُ اللَّهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ أَنْ يَعْقِدَ شَعِيرَةً وَ مَا هُوَ بِعَاقِدِهَا» وَ نَهَى عَنِ التَّصَاوِيرِ وَقَالَ «مَنْ صَوَّرَ صُورَةً كَلَّفَهُ اللَّهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ أَنْ يَنْفُخَ فِيهَا وَ لَيْسَ بِنَافِخٍ» وَ نَهَى أَنْ يُحْرَقَ شَيْءٌ مِنَ الْحَيَوَانِ بِالنَّارِ وَ نَهَى عَنْ سَبِّ الدِّيكِ وَقَالَ «إِنَّهُ يُوقِظُ لِلصَّلَاةِ» وَ نَهَى أَنْ يَدْخُلَ الرَّجُلُ فِي سَوْمِ أَخِيهِ الْمُسْلِمِ وَ نَهَى أَنْ يُكْثَرَ الْكَلامُ عِنْدَ الْمُجَامَعَةِ وَقَالَ «يَكُونُ مِنْهُ خَرَسُ الْوَلَدِ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He forbade wailing loudly during calamities and prohibited lamentation and listening to it. He forbade women from following funeral processions. He prohibited wiping off anything from the Book of Allah with saliva or writing with it. He forbade a man from intentionally lying about his dreams and said: 'Allah will burden him on the Day of Judgment to tie a grain of barley, and he will not be able to do so.' He prohibited making images and said: 'Whoever creates an image, Allah will task him on the Day of Judgment to breathe life into it, and he will not be able to do so.' He forbade burning any living creature with fire. He prohibited cursing the rooster and said: 'Indeed, it awakens for prayer.' He forbade a man from interfering in the sale of his Muslim brother. He prohibited excessive talking during intimate relations and said: 'It results in a child being born mute.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "و قَالَ «لَا تُبَيِّتُوا الْقُمَامَةَ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ وَأَخْرِجُوهَا نَهَارًا فَإِنَّهَا مَقْعَدُ الشَّيْطَانِ» وَ قَالَ «لَا يَبِيتَنَّ أَحَدُكُمْ وَ يَدُهُ غَمِرَةٌ فَإِنْ فَعَلَ فَأَصَابَهُ لَمَمُ الشَّيْطَانِ فَلَا يَلُومَنَّ إِلَّا نَفْسَهُ» وَ نَهَى أَنْ يَسْتَنْجِيَ الرَّجُلُ بِالرَّوْثِ وَ الرِّمَّةِ وَ نَهَى أَنْ تَخْرُجَ الْمَرْأَةُ مِنْ بَيْتِهَا بِغَيْرِ إِذْنِ زَوْجِهَا فَإِنْ خَرَجَتْ لَعَنَهَا كُلُّ مَلَكٍ فِي السَّمَاءِ وَ كُلُّ شَيْءٍ تَمُرُّ عَلَيْهِ مِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنْسِ حَتَّى تَرْجِعَ إِلَى بَيْتِهَا وَ نَهَى أَنْ تَتَزَيَّنَ لِغَيْرِ زَوْجِهَا «فَإِنْ فَعَلَتْ كَانَ حَقًّا عَلَى اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ أَنْ يُحْرِقَهَا بِالنَّارِ» وَ نَهَى أَنْ تَتَكَلَّمَ الْمَرْأَةُ عِنْدَ غَيْرِ زَوْجِهَا أَوْ غَيْرِ ذِي مَحْرَمٍ مِنْهَا أَكْثَرَ مِنْ خَمْسِ كَلِمَاتٍ مِمَّا لَا بُدَّ لَهَا مِنْهُ وَ نَهَى أَنْ تُبَاشِرَ الْمَرْأَةُ الْمَرْأَةَ وَ لَيْسَ بَيْنَهُمَا ثَوْبٌ وَ نَهَى أَنْ تُحَدِّثَ الْمَرْأَةُ الْمَرْأَةَ بِمَا تَخْلُو بِهِ مَعَ زَوْجِهَا وَ نَهَى أَنْ يُجَامِعَ الرَّجُلُ أَهْلَهُ مُسْتَقْبِلَ الْقِبْلَةِ وَعَلَى ظَهْرِ طَرِيقٍ عَامِرٍ «فَمَنْ فَعَلَ ذَلِكَ فَعَلَيْهِ لَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ وَالْمَلَائِكَةِ وَالنَّاسِ أَجْمَعِينَ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He said: 'Do not leave garbage in your homes overnight. Take it out during the day, for it is the seat of Satan.' He said: 'Let none of you sleep while his hand is unwashed from grease. If he does and something harmful happens to him from Satan, he should blame no one but himself.' He forbade a man from performing istinja with dung or bones. He forbade a woman from leaving her house without her husband's permission. If she does, every angel in the sky and everything she passes from among the jinn and humans will curse her until she returns to her home. He forbade a woman from adorning herself for anyone other than her husband, saying: 'If she does so, it becomes a right upon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to burn her in the Fire.' He prohibited a woman from speaking to a man who is not her husband or a mahram more than five necessary words. He forbade a woman from directly touching another woman without a cloth between them. He forbade women from describing their intimate relations with their husbands to other women. He prohibited a man from having intimate relations with his wife while facing the Qiblah or on a public road. He said: 'Whoever does so, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "و نَهَى «أَنْ يَقُولَ الرَّجُلُ لِلرَّجُلِ زَوِّجْنِي أُخْتَكَ حَتَّى أُزَوِّجَكَ أُخْتِي» وَ نَهَى عَنْ إِتْيَانِ الْعَرَّافِ وَقَالَ «مَنْ أَتَاهُ وَ صَدَّقَهُ فَقَدْ بَرِئَ مِمَّا أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ» وَ نَهَى عَنِ اللَّعِبِ بِالنَّرْدِ وَالشِّطْرَنْجِ وَالْكُوبَةِ وَالْعَرْطَبَةِ وَ هِيَ الطُّنْبُورُ وَالْعُودُ وَ نَهَى عَنِ الْغِيبَةِ وَالِاسْتِمَاعِ إِلَيْهَا وَ نَهَى عَنِ النَّمِيمَةِ وَالِاسْتِمَاعِ إِلَيْهَا وَقَالَ «لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ قَتَّاتٌ» يَعْنِي نَمَّامًا وَ نَهَى عَنْ إِجَابَةِ الْفَاسِقِينَ إِلَى طَعَامِهِمْ وَ نَهَى عَنِ الْيَمِينِ الْكَاذِبَةِ وَقَالَ «إِنَّهَا تَتْرُكُ الدِّيَارَ بَلاَقِعَ» وَقَالَ «مَنْ حَلَفَ بِيَمِينٍ كَاذِبَةٍ صَبْرًا لِيَقْطَعَ بِهَا مَالَ امْرِئٍ مُسْلِمٍ لَقِيَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ وَ هُوَ عَلَيْهِ غَضْبَانُ إِلَّا أَنْ يَتُوبَ وَ يَرْجِعَ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He forbade a man from saying to another man, 'Marry me your sister, and I will marry you mine.' He prohibited visiting fortune-tellers and said: 'Whoever visits one and believes in them has disbelieved in what Allah revealed to Muhammad.' He forbade playing with dice, chess, drums, and stringed instruments (lute and oud). He forbade backbiting and listening to it, as well as gossiping and listening to it. He said: 'A tale-bearer will not enter Paradise.' He forbade accepting invitations to the meals of corrupt individuals. He prohibited taking false oaths and said: 'Indeed, false oaths leave lands desolate.' He said: 'Whoever swears a false oath deliberately to unlawfully seize the wealth of a Muslim will meet Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him - unless he repents and returns the right.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "و نَهَى عَنِ الْجُلُوسِ عَلَى مَائِدَةٍ يُشْرَبُ عَلَيْهَا الْخَمْرُ وَ نَهَى أَنْ يُدْخِلَ الرَّجُلُ حَلِيلَتَهُ إِلَى الْحَمَّامِ وَقَالَ «لَا يَدْخُلَنَّ أَحَدُكُمُ الْحَمَّامَ إِلَّا بِمِئْزَرٍ» وَ نَهَى عَنِ الْمُحَادَثَةِ الَّتِي تَدْعُو إِلَى غَيْرِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ وَ نَهَى عَنْ تَصْفِيقِ الْوَجْهِ وَ نَهَى عَنِ الشُّرْبِ فِي آنِيَةِ الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ وَ نَهَى عَنْ لُبْسِ الْحَرِيرِ وَالْدِّيبَاجِ وَالْقَزِّ لِلرِّجَالِ فَأَمَّا لِلنِّسَاءِ فَلَا بَأْسَ وَ نَهَى أَنْ تُبَاعَ الثِّمَارُ حَتَّى تَزْهُوَ يَعْنِي تَصْفَرَّ أَوْ تَحْمَرَّ وَ نَهَى عَنِ الْمُحَاقَلَةِ يَعْنِي بَيْعَ التَّمْرِ بِالرُّطَبِ وَالزَّبِيبِ بِالْعِنَبِ وَ مَا أَشْبَهَ ذَلِكَ وَ نَهَى عَنْ بَيْعِ النَّرْدِ وَ أَنْ يُشْتَرَى الْخَمْرُ وَ أَنْ يُسْقَى الْخَمْرُ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He forbade sitting at a table where alcohol is being consumed. He prohibited a man from taking his wife into the bathhouse and said: 'Let none of you enter the bathhouse without wearing a waistcloth.' He forbade conversations that lead to anything other than the remembrance of Allah. He prohibited slapping the face and drinking from gold and silver vessels. He forbade men from wearing silk, brocade, and fine silk, though it is permissible for women. He forbade selling fruits before they ripen (turn yellow or red). He prohibited muhaqala (selling dates for fresh dates and raisins for grapes or similar transactions). He forbade selling dice games and purchasing or serving alcohol."
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "و قَالَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ «لَعَنَ اللَّهُ الْخَمْرَ وَ غَارِسَهَا وَ عَاصِرَهَا وَ شَارِبَهَا وَ سَاقِيَهَا وَ بَائِعَهَا وَ مُشْتَرِيَهَا وَ آكِلَ ثَمَنِهَا وَ حَامِلَهَا وَالْمَحْمُولَةَ إِلَيْهِ» وَقَالَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ «مَنْ شَرِبَهَا لَمْ يَقْبَلِ اللَّهُ لَهُ صَلَاةً أَرْبَعِينَ يَوْمًا فَإِنْ مَاتَ وَ فِي بَطْنِهِ شَيْءٌ مِنْ ذَلِكَ كَانَ حَقًّا عَلَى اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ أَنْ يَسْقِيَهُ مِنْ طِينَةِ خَبَالٍ وَ هِيَ صَدِيدُ أَهْلِ النَّارِ وَ مَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْ فُرُوجِ الزُّنَاةِ فَيَجْتَمِعُ ذَلِكَ فِي قُدُورِ جَهَنَّمَ فَيَشْرَبُهُ أَهْلُ النَّارِ فَ يُصْهَرُ بِهِ مَا فِي بُطُونِهِمْ وَالْجُلُودُ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He (as) said: 'May Allah curse alcohol, its planter, its presser, its drinker, its server, its seller, its buyer, the one who consumes its price, its carrier, and the one to whom it is carried.' He (as) also said: 'Whoever drinks it, Allah will not accept his prayer for forty days. If he dies with any of it in his stomach, it becomes a right upon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to make him drink from the mud of filth, which is the pus of the people of Hell and what comes out of the private parts of the adulterers. This mixture will collect in the cauldrons of Hell, and the people of Hell will drink it, causing their insides and skins to melt.'"
      }
    },
